    "read_order": [
      "Positive i32 request and nonnull reader required; otherwise return INT32_MIN before budget.",
      "Call underlying reader+20 seek(accessor.sourceCursor). If its returned i64 differs: return -2147483645 only for that exact transient code, otherwise INT32_MIN. First-byte and converter untouched on this path.",
      "Call accessor+188 needs-conversion. Concrete10036fb74 compares rate, bit depth, frame bytes, kind, layout, channels, extra format and gain1. No mismatch: reader+10 reads requested count directly; positive result advances sourceCursor by that count, else no cursor advance. Does not consume first byte.",
      "Conversion: reuse accessor+20; lazily allocate0xb0/1003237d8(policy+49) only if absent. Refresh source format through100323904(stream+10), destination through100323b24(accessor+10), copy gain to converter+28.",
      "Compute budget100330d84(request, firstByte); save oldFirst and clear accessor+4a immediately. Budget<1 returns0 without source read/conversion, keeping consumed first status.",
      "Allocate source-format storage for budget; underlying reader+10 reads budget. Negative source result returns unchanged numeric error; no accessor cursor advance, but firstByte remains0.",
      "For nonnegative source result, rate mismatch computes terminal=(reader.tell>=source.length)&&oldFirst&&(budget>sourceRead). Equal rates force terminalfalse.",
      "Pass actual source count by reference to100330cd4(destination, sourceStorage, &count, terminal). Success: advance sourceCursor by original actual SOURCE count if nonzero, return rewritten count. Failure: return INT32_MIN; accessor cursor unchanged, first remains0, and underlying source may already have advanced. No transactional rollback of backend/source state is established."
